        "id": "ch14_3_3-2",
        "text": "Amazon (starting in 2017), called Lightsail . This service was introduced in order to offer clients an\neasy way to deploy virtual private servers ( VPSs ) or VMs in the cloud. The interface is similar to\nthat seen from the competition, but it comes with the full Amazon infrastructure reliability on top.\nLightsail provides several distributions, together with application bundles. Deploying on AWS, using\nLightsail, becomes more straightforward. It is a useful tool to lure in new users wanting a quick and\nsecure solution for delivering their web apps.\nThere are other solutions available, such as Google\u2019s solution, called GCE, which is the IaaS solution from\nGoogle Cloud Platform ( GCP ). The GCP interface is very similar to the one on the Azure platform.\nImportant note\nOne interesting aspect of using GCP is that when you want to delete a project, the operation\nis not immediate, and the deletion is scheduled in one month\u2019s time. This could be seen as a\nsafety net if the deletion was not intentional, and you need to roll back the project.\nIn the next section, we will detail some of the PaaS solutions.",
